        <mxCell id="skeys" value="other Agents keys and connections" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="790" y="470" width="320" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note" value="&lt;b&gt;FULL_ISOLATION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The left frame is created at run time by the Agent Provisioner and destroyed by Lifecycle Manager Cleanup. Terraform does not own it.&lt;br&gt;sa-agent-finance-001 may invoke dedicated-op-finance-001 and nothing else. sa-op-finance-001 may sign with the dedicated key only.&lt;br&gt;The dedicated ID-JAG key still sits in the shared issuer JWKS, so a leaked key forges the same range as a shared one.&lt;br&gt;What shrinks is how many Registrations and Refresh Tokens one breach reaches, not the forging power.&lt;br&gt;Dashed: created only when enable_google_bridge=true." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=2;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
